      "id": 18684,
      "name": "Nagnazul",
      "username": "Nagnazul",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/ecccb3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-10-26T05:23:52.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>In a 2-player game, let's say both players are doing growth and pick a growth option that involves gaining a power. Is it within the rules for player 1 to look at 4 minor powers, then player 2 to look at the next 4 minor powers&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;player 1 makes a choice? Having that extra information can be helpful for making a decision, but I'd like to know if that's within the rules. Wouldn't want to cheat while playing at the highest difficulties :)</p>\n<p>Thanks!</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:07.142Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 4,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
