      "id": 223799,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-10-26T13:37:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I do that all the time so I certainly <em>hope </em>it's okay ;). And all too often I compare my four cards to those of the other person and grumble about how we should've drawn our four cards the other way around so that we each actually got options that involve our Elements and stuff :P. But yeah, as far as I'm aware there's no reason to wait for another player to pick their card before you draw four for yourself to choose from. And obviously you can only choose a card from the four you've drawn - you can't look at someone else's (or have them look at yours) and pick one of those ;).</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:02.258Z",
