      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nagnazul\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/ecccb3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nagnazul:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In a 2-player game, let’s say both players are doing growth and pick a growth option that involves gaining a power. Is it within the rules for player 1 to look at 4 minor powers, then player 2 to look at the next 4 minor powers&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;player 1 makes a choice? Having that extra information can be helpful for making a decision, but I’d like to know if that’s within the rules.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yup, totally fine!</p>",
